id: pmc-x0u4
title: Replace hand-built api doubles in extension tests with the SDK activation harness
description: "pm-changelog never carried the defineExtension any-shim so it fell outside the 2026.7.26 typed-authoring rollout, but its extension tests still built api doubles by hand and cast them through Parameters of extension.activate. Those doubles verify the extension against a locally captured object rather than the host contract, and skip the capability governance pm applies at activation."
type: Task
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-07-26T09:02:36.095Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-26T09:02:42.985Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-26T09:02:42.984Z"
author: codex
acceptance_criteria: "Registration, flag and renderer-ownership assertions read from the real activation result; Handler-invoking tests run through runRegisteredCommandForTest; The legacy two-argument runtime test keeps a documented double because it simulates a different host version; Full suite passes and the extension is functionally verified in a real workspace"
resolution: "Migrated five of six hand-built api doubles onto activateExtensionForTest and runRegisteredCommandForTest, with the capability grant read from manifest.json. The sixth is retained and documented because its subject is the legacy two-argument registerExporter host, which the harness cannot simulate."
expected_result: "Extension surface verified against the real host contract under manifest capability governance, with no behavior change."
actual_result: 179/179 tests pass; typecheck clean; functional install confirmed pm changelog generate and pm changelog export --format json both run against a real workspace.
close_reason: Implemented and verified
body: ""
